{"reference":"Isaiah 4","book":"Isaiah","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Isaiah in Its Larger Textual Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Isaiah 4 is part of a book preserved in the Great Isaiah Scroll, an almost complete witness to all sixty-six chapters. It is broadly aligned with the Masoretic tradition, though it contains many spelling and substantive differences. Other Isaiah manuscripts and interpretive writings from Qumran also show that the book was actively copied and interpreted.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_004_8fca6aae22eaa0e168ea75da"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}